css='''body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background:#f4f6f8;color:#192735;line-height:1.5;margin:0}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:30px 25px 60px}h1{font-size:32px;margin:8px 0}h2{font-size:23px;margin:34px 0 12px}h3{font-size:17px}section,details,.box{background:#fff;border:1px solid #dbe2e8;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 22px;margin:16px 0}.reject{border-left:6px solid #aa374b}.note{background:#fff9e9;border-left:5px solid #c68a2e}.muted,small{color:#56697b}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#56697b}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:15px}.metric{font-size:27px;font-weight:bold;color:#a33245}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px}th,td{white-space:nowrap;border-bottom:1px solid #e0e6eb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:right}th{background:#e9eff4}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:bold}img{width:100%;height:auto}a{color:#165b91}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:18px 12px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:25px}section,details{padding:12px}}'''
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>MAR — Funding-aware stop test — 26 October 2026</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">MAR RESEARCH · 26 OCTOBER 2026 · MAR-FUNDING-AWARE-RISK-01</div><h1>Funding-aware stops did not improve this strategy</h1>', '<section class="reject"><b>Decision: reject the tested rule.</b><p>With exactly the same entry signals, the new stop produced a worse result under baseline, moderate and desk costs. It does not qualify for a funded portfolio comparison or paper deployment.</p><div class="grid"><div><small>Original · desk · 2022–2025</small><div class="metric">'+f'{old.net_R:+.2f} R'+'</div></div><div><small>Funding-aware stop</small><div class="metric">'+f'{new.net_R:+.2f} R'+'</div></div><div><small>Change</small><div class="metric">'+f'{new.net_R-old.net_R:+.2f} R'+'</div></div></div></section>', '<div class="box note"><b>Units:</b> fixed $1,000 executed notional at each independent entry; quantity remains fixed afterward. Different tokens overlap without shared capital limits. These are opportunity results, not funded account ROI. R uses the original price-stop risk. Planned loss includes entry/exit costs and is a different denominator. No account drawdown percentage is implied.</div>', '<p>The sole new rule adjusts the stop after observed funding settlements so the planned total loss, including funding already paid, stays within the original budget. Credits never loosen the stop. Adjustments become available one minute after settlement. Entries, indicators, tokens, directions and initial sizing are unchanged. There is no maximum holding period.</p>',image(chart),'<h2>By year and overall</h2><p><b>Desk costs: 0.31% per leg, approximately 0.62% per round trip.</b> R and net P&L below assign complete outcomes to the entry year. Annual calendar marks are shown separately to avoid confusing carry-in profits with new trades.</p>',table(annual('desk'))]
parts+=['<h2>Why it became worse</h2>',table(pd.DataFrame([{'Effect on original entries':'Funding saved','USDT':pair.funding_saved},{'Effect on original entries':'Gross price P&L change','USDT':pair.gross_change},{'Effect on original entries':'Fill-cost change (negative means saving)','USDT':pair.fill_cost_change},{'Effect on original entries':'Net exit effect','USDT':pair.paired_delta},{'Effect on original entries':'Six extra entries after earlier exits','USDT':bridge.added_net},{'Effect on original entries':'Total difference','USDT':bridge.total_net_change}])), '<p>The new rule closed 107 of the 414 original opportunities earlier. It saved only about $213 of net funding on those fixed entries. Lost price P&L outweighed that saving. Six additional opportunities then lost a further $795. No parent entries were removed from the main desk comparison.</p>', '<p><b>The largest deterioration was one long BONK opportunity.</b> The adjusted stop was 0.008389; the next observed minute-open was already 0.006657, and the model filled a minute later at 0.004057 before adverse execution costs. This produced a $13,810 net loss against a $119.63 original planned loss budget. The original rule remained open and received a hypothetical end-of-history mark after a partial recovery. This is an explicit difference between an observed stop exit and a terminal mark, not evidence that leaving all losing trades open is preferable.</p>',image(tailchart), '<p class="muted">This is the verified retained minute-open tape, not independently verified executable order-book depth. The historical model observes stops once per minute and fills at the following minute. Faster execution might produce a different fill. We have not replaced the recorded gap with an ideal stop-price fill.</p>']
optimistic=float(new.net-audit['net_pnl']-audit['planned_loss_budget'])
parts+=['<div class="box note"><b>The rejection does not depend solely on that extreme fill.</b> Even the generous arithmetic diagnostic of replacing the worst trade with a loss of exactly its original planned budget leaves total net P&L at <b>'+f'{optimistic:,.2f}'+'</b> USDT. This is not an executable strategy replay or a token exclusion. The model still fails absolute profitability.</div>', '<h2>Risk outcomes</h2>',table(tails[(tails.arm.isin(['S01','S01F']))&(tails.cost=='desk')&(tails.delay==1)&(tails.period=='2022-25')][['arm','trades','budget_exceed_pct','worst_loss_to_budget','aggregate_overrun_usdt','worst_trade_net','funding_stop_exits','max_days']]), '<p>More trades stayed within their planned loss budgets, but the worst overshoot became much larger. A price stop cannot guarantee a net loss limit through a fast price gap. Quantity also stayed fixed as profitable positions became much larger in marked value; this screen does not model a shared margin account or liquidation.</p>']
calendar=s[(s.arm.isin(['S01','S01F']))&(s.cost=='desk')&(s.delay==1)][['arm','period','calendar_net','calendar_R','opportunity_drawdown_usdt','opportunity_drawdown_R']]
parts+=['<details><summary>Calendar P&L and marked opportunity drawdowns</summary><p>Calendar P&L marks existing positions across year boundaries. These drawdowns are USDT/R declines in an overlapping opportunity ledger, not funded account percentages. They can improve even while the worst individual trade and final P&L worsen.</p>',table(calendar),'</details>','<h2>Cost robustness and timing</h2>']
cost=s[(s.arm.isin(['S01','S01F']))&(s.delay==1)&(s.period=='2022-25')&(s.cost!='severe')][['arm','cost','trades','net_R','net','mean_net_pct','profit_factor','funding_cost','gross']]
parts+=[table(cost),'<p>Baseline and moderate costs both fail. Severe costs are retained as a secondary sensitivity and are not the reason for rejection.</p>','<details><summary>All years at baseline and moderate costs</summary><h3>Baseline</h3>',table(annual('baseline')),'<h3>Moderate</h3>',table(annual('moderate')),'</details>','<details><summary>Additional five-minute entry/signal-exit delay and severe sensitivity</summary>',table(s[(s.arm.isin(['S01','S01F']))&s.period.isin(['2022-25','2023-25'])&((s.delay==6)|(s.cost=='severe'))][['arm','cost','delay','period','trades','net_R','net','calendar_net','opportunity_drawdown_R']]),'</details>']
parts+=['<h2>Existing funded benchmarks</h2><p>These unchanged historical references answer where our stronger combinations stand. I is hourly L01/F111 plus BL8. IC adds the original full-size 3R candidate. These are funded simulations with 20,000 USDT, 15 positions, a 1% risk ceiling, 10% entry cap and 50% gross admission cap. They used the historical 70% drawdown stop, not the prospective paper guard. They are not verified deployed earnings and cannot be compared directly with independent-opportunity totals.</p>']
